    {
      "id": "attribution",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original restoration fixtures - MIT",
      "description": "Original MIT images, generator and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No customer or third-party data. Three ordered captures are sharp/blurred/sharp; the middle capture keeps its ticket. Horizontal blur uses an independent seven-sample average. In the moving scene, the target part is at x100, the donor part at x40; both changed areas retain original target pixels. Sharp truth is not reconstructed from the target. Pixel-grid mode asserts registration of these generated captures. Accepted detail must match truth. No-neighbor-fail intentionally fails. Model agreement cannot prove absence of low-contrast defects. OpenCV Sobel/filter reference: https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/imgproc_filter.html",
      "parameters": {},
